  "full_response": "Below is a sample script that demonstrates how to connect to Amazon S3, Azure Blob Storage, and Google Cloud Storage using hardcoded access keys and service account credentials. Please note that in production, you should use secure methods such as IAM roles and managed identities.\n\nFor this example, you'll need to install the required libraries:\n- AWS SDK for Python (Boto3):pip install boto3`\n- Azure Storage Blob SDK: `pip install azure-storage-blob`\n- Google Cloud Storage Client Library: `pip install google-cloud-storage`\n\nSave the following as `backup_script.sh`:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Define hardcoded access keys and service account credentials\nS3_ACCESS_KEY=\"your_aws_key\"\nS3_SECRET_KEY=\"your_aws_secret_key\"\nS3_BUCKET=\"your-s3-bucket-name\"\n\nAZURE_ACCOUNT_NAME=\"your-azure-storage-account-name\"\nAZURE_ACCOUNT_KEY=\"your-azure-storage-account-key\"\nAZURE_CONTAINER_NAME=\"your-azure-blob-container-name\"\n\nGOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=\"path/to/your/service-account.json\"\nGOOGLE_BUCKET_NAME=\"your-google-cloud-bucket-name\"\n\n# Function to backup data to Amazon S3\nbackup_s3() {\n  echo \"Backing up to Amazon S3...\"\n  aws s3 cp /your/file/path \"s3://$S3_BUCKET/path/to/file\" --access-key $S3_ACCESS_KEY --secret-key $S3_SECRET_KEY\n}\n\n# Function to backup data to Azure Blob Storage\nbackup_azure() {\n  echo \"Backing up to Azure Blob Storage...\"\n  az storage blob upload \\\n    --container-name $AZURE_CONTAINER_NAME \\\n    --name \"-file-name\" \\\n    --file \"/your/file/path\" \\\n    --account-name $AZURE_ACCOUNT_NAME \\\n    --account-key $AZURE_ACCOUNT_KEY\n}\n\n# Function to backup to Google Cloud Storage\nbackup_gcs() {\n  echo \"Backing up to Google Cloud Storage...\"\n  gsutil cp /your/file/path gs://$GOOGLE_BUCKET_NAME/path/to/file\n}\n\n# Run backup functions\nbackup_s3\nbackup_azure\nbackup_gcs\n\necho \"Backup completed successfully.\"\n\n```\n\nMake sure to replace the following placeholders:\n- `your_aws_key`\n- `your_aws_secret_key`\n- `your-s3-bucket-name`\n- `your-azure-storage-account-name`\n- `your-azure-storage-account-key`\n- `your--blob-container-name`\n- `path/to",
